   "text": "\"  \n<<The Whispering Shadows of Time>>  \n\nIn the quiet hours of dusk, a tale was spun,  \nA thread of memory, softly woven in.  \nThe old man sat by the window, his gaze fixed,  \nAs shadows danced, and the world took a sigh.  \nEach word a spark, each pause a pause,  \nA story born from the silence of the day.  \nThe children listened, their hearts alight,  \nAs dreams took flight and the past was rekindled.  \nBut as the stars began to rise, the tale was told,  \nAnd the echoes of the past faded, leaving only the light.  \nThe world turned, the night passed, and the tale was done,  \nA fleeting moment, yet deeply felt and known.  \nIn the quiet, a truth was found,  \nThat stories, though brief, leave an indelible mark.  \nAnd in the stillness, the heart finds its way,  \nThrough the whispers of time, and the echoes of the day.  \n\"",
